; lifecycle-atomic-reload: the bad carrier. It was packed against a join
; that includes `ghost`, so its bytes are valid; loading it against the good
; join (which lacks `ghost`) is a registry-identity refusal, reason 9. The
; old score stays live, which is what the lifecycle steps pin.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4])

(track :target ghost
  (key :at 0b :value 0.5))
